<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Qianshuiyuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">618</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transition-from-sui-to-tang">Transition from Sui to Tang</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Qianshuiyuan was fought in 618 in the north of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> between the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-ju">Xue Ju</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-rengao">Xue Rengao</a>. In the summer, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> lay ill, Qin forces routed a Tang army there; in the autumn Li Shimin returned, waited until Qin supplies ran short and then destroyed Xue Rengao's army. Xue Rengao surrendered and was executed, opening the north-west to the Tang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-qianshuiyuan.jpg" alt="Battle of Qianshuiyuan" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Establishment_of_the_Tang_Dynasty.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
